Mr. Whitlatch,<br />
<br />
This is the firm's complete response to Item 4 of the staff's deficiency le=
tter of April 27, 2011 in examination 2011-0463. The signed letter is attac=
hed and this message sets out its substance.<br />
<br />
Vandergrift Rowe accepts Item 4. Effective May 27, 2011 all 168 affected cl=
ient accounts have been transferred to Wexbury Fiduciary Trust, a qualified=
 custodian unaffiliated with the firm, under custodial agreements that give=
 Vandergrift Rowe no authority to withdraw funds or securities. The firm ha=
s discontinued the direct fee-debit instruction described in Item 4 across =
all client accounts.<br />
<br />
Vandergrift Rowe further undertakes to obtain the surprise examination requ=
ired by Rule 206(4)-2(a)(4) by an independent public accountant, with the c=
orresponding Form ADV-E filing, for any period within the term of this unde=
rtaking in which the firm is deemed to have custody of client funds or secu=
rities. This undertaking is given for calendar years 2011 and 2012 and shal=
l expire by its terms on December 31, 2012.<br />
<br />
Pemberton Ivey LLP has been engaged to perform the examination for calendar=
 year 2011 and the Form ADV-E will be filed within 120 days of the examinat=
ion date.<br />
<br />
Please treat this letter as the corrective action commitment on which the s=
taff's closing of examination 2011-0463 is conditioned.<br />
